AI Search & UGV Navigation Assignment
This repository contains three AI/search implementations developed in Python using Google Colab/Jupyter Notebook.
Contents
1. Dijkstra's Shortest Path – Finds the shortest route between two Indian cities.
2. UGV Navigation using A* – Finds a path for an Unmanned Ground Vehicle through a grid containing obstacles.
3. UGV Navigation with Dynamic Obstacles – Uses A* repeatedly so the UGV can re-plan when new obstacles appear.

Assignment 1 – Dijkstra's Shortest Path

Finds the shortest route between two Indian cities.
Uses Dijkstra's Algorithm.
Uses city distance as the edge weight.
Dataset: indian-cities-dataset.csv

Assignment 2 – UGV Navigation

Finds a path for an Unmanned Ground Vehicle (UGV) in a 70×70 grid.
Uses A* Search with Manhattan distance.
Supports low, medium, and high obstacle densities.
Allows movement in four directions: up, down, left, and right.

Assignment 3 – Dynamic UGV Navigation

Extends UGV navigation to handle dynamic obstacles.
Uses A* Search with re-planning.
New obstacles can appear while the UGV is moving.
If the path is blocked, a new path is calculated automatically.

Technologies Used

Python
Google Colab / Jupyter Notebook
Pandas
Heap Queue (heapq)
Random
